\par \pard\li355\fi-175 \b 
\par \cf1 Bioderm\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 the Bioderms are similar to clones. The DNA sample they are cloned from is incorporated into a protoplasm to form a base genetic matrix (BGM).  The DNA samples come from former human heroes. In the\plain\fs20  \uldb \cf2 Bioderm Facility\plain\fs20\cf2 {\v GCVAN7}\cf1 , you  may preview a catalogue of BGMs to create a Bioderm. 
\par \pard\li265\fi-85 \plain\fs20 
\par \b\cf1 Bioderm Facility\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 this is an area of the Herc Base where you can create and administer to Bioderms; this is also where you train Bioderms and biomechanically link them to Hercs.
\par 
\par \b Biovat\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 the area inside the Bioderm Facility where Bioderms are created.
\par \b 
\par Communications\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 with each promotion, you receive communications from Unitech Command; these communications tell you something about the number and types of Hercs and Bioderms you are allowed to command, and any new technology available to you.
\par \pard\li265\fi-85 
\par \b Cybrid\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 the enemy equivalent to the Herculan; Cybrids are currently manufactured in eight models: Specter, Parasite, Cerebrus, Arachnus, Genocite, Malignus, Hades, and Nihilus.
\par 
\par \b Genetic Stability\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 all Bioderm\'92s have a Genetic Stability rating which is a function of the way they were created; Bioderms start completely stable upon creation; Stability deteriorates as a Bioderm\'92s Herc takes hits during battle or as\plain\fs20  \uldb \cf2 Stimgland\plain\fs20\cf2 {\v 4GI42I}\plain\fs20  \cf1 is administered; once Genetic Stability reaches half of its maximum, Skill Ratings begin to drop. Genetic Stability can be restored with the Stabilize option in the Medvat.
\par \pard\li265\fi-85 
\par \b Herc\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 short for Herculan; the monolithic fighting machines employed by Unitech Command; currently, eight models are manufactured: Shadow, Remora, Sensei, Ogre, Giant, Demon, Reaper, and Juggernaut.
\par 
\par \b Herc Base\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 this is the main station from which you perform all inter-battle activities; from here, you can access the Bioderm Facility, Herc Bay, and the Herc Command Center; you also launch all missions from the Herc Base.
\par 
\par \b Herc Bay\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 this is the area of the Herc Base where you purchase and maintain your Hercs.
\par \pard\li265\fi-85 
\par \b Herc Carrier\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 your transportation into any new mission and back to the Herc Base; you can also \'93hide\'94 your Hercs here during battle (although once re-boarded, they cannot return to the battle).
\par 
\par \b Herc Command Center\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 this is the area of the Herc Base where you select your missions, observe your Career Status, or review previous Corporate Communications.
\par 
\par \b Jackup\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 a variety of the Stimgland meta-steroid that increases all percentages in a Bioderm\'92s Skill Ratings (except for Command) for a set number of turns; also adds to a Bioderm\'92s Toxin level.
\par \pard\li265\fi-85 
\par \b Link\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 the area inside the Bioderm Facility where Bioderms are biomechanically linked to Hercs.
\par 
\par \b Medvat\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 the area inside the Bioderm Facility where you take Bioderms to regenerate their health, balance Genetic Stability, and detoxify them; this is also where they can be recycled.
\par 
\par \b Ore\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 valuable deposits of ore are found on most of the planets and moons in the Cyberstorm Universe; what makes ore so valuable is that it is not a naturally occurring mineral, but fossilized slag left behind by a technological civilization that disappeared millions of years ago; Ore is actually a complex mix of dozens of valuable heavy metals, rare elements, and most exciting, stable trans-uranic elements not found in nature, and beyond the reach of human technology.  
\par \pard\li265\fi-85 
\par \b Placidex\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 a variety of the Stimgland meta-steroid that rejuvenates a Bioderm\'92s Stability; also adds to a Bioderm\'92s Toxin level.
\par 
\par \b Stimgland\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 either of the two meta-steroids, Jackup or Placidex, that are administered in the Pilot Status area while out on a mission.
\par 
\par \b Toxins\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 these are introduced into Bioderms as Stimgland is administered; once Toxin levels reach the Bioderm\'92s tolerance threshold, Health begins to deteriorate; Toxins can be removed in the Medvat.
\par \pard\li265\fi-85 
\par \b VREC \'96 Virtual Reality Enhancement Center\plain\fs20\cf1  \'96 the area inside the Bioderm Facility where Bioderms are trained to enhance all Skill Ratings: Piloting, Energy, Missile, Cannon, Plasma, ELF, Advanced Tech., and Command).
\par \pard \plain\fs20 
\par }